member.summary:
Base of a dependent mod's  class. RimWorld finds the subclass by Type; its name decides the settings file
name (Mod_<folder>_<TypeName>.xml), so an existing mod keeps its old class name.

public sealed class LOMod : KitModBase
{
    public LOMod(ModContentPack c) : base(c, new KitInfo { Name = "Luciferium Overhaul", ShortId = "LO", Version = "2.0.0", PerSave = true }) { }
    protected override void Register(KitRegistry r) { r.Section("healing", "Healing"); r.Float("healing", "Regrowth", "lo.regrowDays", 10f, 0.1f, 120f, "Days to regrow a limb"); }
}

The base constructor does everything in this order: context, log header, API-level check, , settings file
(with legacy migration), the mod's Harmony patch classes one by one. Fields of the subclass are not set yet while Register runs.
Every hook below runs inside the mod's error fence; an exception never reaches the game or another mod.

Window sizing for every window of a mod. Windows declare the size they were designed for at a 900 px tall screen;
 scales it up for larger screens and by the player's global "Window size" preference (Mod settings,
JB Framework), and never lets it leave the screen. Usage: public override Vector2 InitialSize => KitUI.Size(900f, 640f);
